<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="NAM" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Nahum</para>
  <para style="mt">Nahum</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The burden of Nineveh <char style="add">[abode of Ninus, or Offspring’s Habitation]</char>. The book of the vision of Nachum <char style="add">[comfort]</char> the Elkoshi <char style="add">[God is ensnarer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> jealous, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> revenges; the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> revenges, and <char style="add">[is]</char> furious; the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will take vengeance on his adversaries, and he reserves <char style="add">[wrath]</char> for his enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> slow to anger, and great in power, and will not at all acquit <char style="add">[the wicked]</char>: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has his way in the whirlwind and in the storm, and the clouds <char style="add">[are]</char> the dust of his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />He rebukes the sea, and makes it dry, and dries up all the rivers: Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char> languishes, and Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, and the flower of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> languishes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />The mountains quake at him, and the hills melt, and the earth is burned at his presence, yes, the world, and all that dwell in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Who can stand before his indignation? and who can abide in the fierceness of his anger? his fury is poured out like fire, and the rocks are thrown down by him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knows them that trust in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But with an overrunning flood he will make an utter end of the place thereof, and darkness shall pursue his enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />What do you<char style="ord">2f</char> imagine against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? he will make an utter end: affliction shall not rise up the second time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For while <char style="add">[they be]</char> folded together <char style="add">[as]</char> thorns, and while they are drunken <char style="add">[as]</char> drunkards, they shall be devoured as stubble fully dry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />There is <char style="add">[one]</char> come out of you<char style="ord">i</char>, that imagines evil against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, a wicked counselor.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Though <char style="add">[they be]</char> quiet, and likewise many, yet thus shall they be cut down, when he shall pass through. Though I have afflicted you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will afflict you<char style="ord">i</char> no more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For now will I break his yoke from off you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will burst your<char style="ord">i</char> bonds in sunder.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has given a commandment concerning you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> no more of your<char style="ord">i</char> name be sown: out of the house of your<char style="ord">i</char> gods will I cut off the graven image and the molten image: I will make your<char style="ord">i</char> grave; for you<char style="ord">i</char> are vile.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Behold upon the mountains the feet of him that brings good tidings, that proclaims peace! O Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, keep your<char style="ord">i</char> solemn feasts, perform your<char style="ord">i</char> vows: for the wicked shall no more pass through you<char style="ord">i</char>; he is utterly cut off.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />He that dashes in pieces is come up before your<char style="ord">i</char> face: keep the munitions, watch the way, make <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> waist strong, fortify <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> power mightily.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has turned away the excellency of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, as the excellency of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for the emptiers have emptied them out, and marred their vine branches.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The shield of his mighty men is made red, the valiant men <char style="add">[are]</char> in scarlet: the chariots <char style="add">[shall be]</char> with flaming torches in the day of his preparation, and the fir trees shall be terribly shaken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The chariots shall rage in the streets, they shall jostle one against another in the broad ways: they shall seem like torches, they shall run like the lightnings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He shall recount his worthies: they shall stumble in their walk; they shall make haste to the wall thereof, and the defense shall be prepared.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The gates of the rivers shall be opened, and the palace shall be dissolved.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And It is fixed. She shall be led away captive, she shall be brought up, and her handmaids shall moan as with the voice of doves, beating upon their breasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But Nineveh [abode of Ninus, or Offspring’s Habitation] <char style="add">[is]</char> of old like a pool of water: yet they shall flee away. Stand, stand, <char style="add">[shall they cry]</char>; but none shall look back.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Take you<char style="ord">2f</char> the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of silver, take the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of gold: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> none end of the store <char style="add">[and]</char> glory out of all the pleasant furniture.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />She is empty, and void, and waste: and the heart melts, and the knees strike together, and much pain <char style="add">[is]</char> in all waist, and the faces of them all gather blackness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Where <char style="add">[is]</char> the dwelling of the lions, and the feeding place of the young lions, where the lion, <char style="add">[even]</char> the old lion, walked, <char style="add">[and]</char> the lion’s whelp <char style="pn">(a cub; a young one)</char>, and none made <char style="add">[them]</char> afraid?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The lion did tear in pieces enough for his whelps, and strangled for his lionesses, and filled his holes with prey, and his dens with ravin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword shall devour your<char style="ord">i</char> young lions: and I will cut off your<char style="ord">i</char> prey from the earth, and the voice of your<char style="ord">i</char> messengers shall no more be heard.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Woe to the bloody city! it <char style="add">[is]</char> all full of lies <char style="add">[and]</char> robbery; the prey departs not;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The noise of a whip, and the noise of the rattling of the wheels, and of the prancing horses, and of the jumping chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The horseman lifts up both the bright sword and the glittering spear: and <char style="add">[there is]</char> a multitude of slain, and a great number of carcasses; and <char style="add">[there is]</char> none end of <char style="add">[their]</char> corpses; they stumble upon their corpses:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Because of the multitude of the cult prostitution of the well-favored prostitute, the mistress of witchcrafts, that sells nations through her cult prostitution, and families through her witchcrafts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; and I will lift your<char style="ord">i</char> skirts over your<char style="ord">i</char> face, and I will show the nations your<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness, and the kingdoms your<char style="ord">i</char> shame.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I will cast abominable filth upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and make you<char style="ord">i</char> vile, and will set you<char style="ord">i</char> as a gazingstock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> all they that look upon you<char style="ord">i</char> shall flee from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and say, Nineveh <char style="add">[abode of Ninus, or Offspring’s Habitation]</char> is laid waste: who will bemoan her? from what place shall I seek comforters for you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Are you<char style="ord">i</char> better than No-Amon <char style="add">[master workman - disrupting]</char>, that was situated among the rivers <char style="pn">(of Egypt)</char>, <char style="add">[that had]</char> the waters round about it, whose fortification <char style="pn">(defensive structure)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> the sea, <char style="add">[and]</char> her wall <char style="add">[was]</char> from the sea?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char> and Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place] [were]</char> her strength, and <char style="add">[it was]</char> infinite; Put <char style="add">[a bow]</char> and Lubim <char style="add">[empty-hearted]</char> were your<char style="ord">i</char> helpers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Yet <char style="add">[was]</char> she carried away, she went into captivity: her young children also were dashed in pieces at the top of all the streets: and they cast lots for her honourable men, and all her great men were bound in chains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> also shall be drunken: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be hid, you<char style="ord">i</char> also shall seek refuge because of the enemy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />All your<char style="ord">i</char> strong holds <char style="add">[shall be like]</char> fig trees with the firstripe figs: if they be shaken, they shall even fall into the mouth of the eater.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> people in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[behave like]</char> women: the gates of your<char style="ord">i</char> land shall be set wide open unto your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies: the fire shall devour your<char style="ord">i</char> bars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Draw yourselfi waters for the siege, fortify your<char style="ord">i</char> strong holds: go into clay, and trample the mortar, make strong the brick factory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />There shall the fire devour you<char style="ord">i</char>; the sword shall cut you<char style="ord">i</char> off, it shall eat you<char style="ord">i</char> up like the cankerworm: make yourself many as the cankerworm, make yourself many as the locusts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have multiplied your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants above the stars of heaven: the cankerworm spoils, and flies away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> guardsmen <char style="add">[are]</char> as the locusts, and your<char style="ord">i</char> captains as the great grasshoppers, which camp in the hedges in the cold day, <char style="add">[but]</char> when the sun arises they flee away, and their place is not known where they <char style="add">[are]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> shepherds slumber, O king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>: your<char style="ord">i</char> nobles shall dwell <char style="add">[in the dust]</char>: your<char style="ord">i</char> people is scattered upon the mountains, and no man gathers <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> no healing of your<char style="ord">i</char> bruise; your<char style="ord">i</char> wound is grievous: all that hear the report of you<char style="ord">i</char> shall clap the hands over you<char style="ord">i</char>: for upon whom has not your<char style="ord">i</char> wickedness passed continually?</para>
</usx>